debloated microduck RL framework

Microduck: ~800 g, 25 cm bipedal robot, 14 Dynamixel XL330 servos. Train
locomotion and tricks in mjlab (MuJoCo Warp) with PPO (rsl_rl), export ONNX,
deploy with the runtime in the microduck repo.

Credit: the robot, the physics and the RL recipes are Pollen Robotics' work --
https://github.com/pollen-robotics/microduck_rl (upstream, Apache-2.0) and
https://github.com/pollen-robotics/microduck (the robot). This fork keeps the
science and drops the scaffolding: no Hugging Face or wandb in the training
path, English-only comments, a flat src/ namespace package with one
task_<name>.py per env, dead code and stale docs removed. Track upstream for
the authoritative version; come here to read the whole thing in an afternoon.

START HERE

Needs a CUDA GPU, uv and make.

    make sync      # install the venv
    make help      # every target, from the smoke test to the ONNX export
    make envs      # every registered task

Then point your coding agent at CLAUDE.md and ask. It documents the tasks, the
env-building workflow, the sim2real invariants and the reward-design rules
that were each learned the hard way -- everything the code does not say out
loud. The rest of this repo is small enough to read.
